{
  "analysis": "We can see the end of doomgeneric_img.c: main calls doomgeneric_Create then loops doomgeneric_Tick, and __start calls main(0,0). We still need the beginning of doomgeneric_img.c (DG_DrawFrame/save logic) and the syscall stubs in my_stdlib.c. The output is truncated, so I'll use smaller ranges and redirect to temp files.",
  "plan": "Print doomgeneric_img.c lines 1-120 and my_stdlib.c syscall-related chunks in small ranges. Also inspect doomgeneric_Tick if present. This will reveal the exact frame saving mechanism and syscalls.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -120 doomgeneric/doomgeneric/doomgeneric_img.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"doomgeneric_Tick\" doomgeneric/doomgeneric/doomgeneric_img.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '121,260p' doomgeneric/doomgeneric/doomgeneric_img.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -nE \"long.*syscall|syscall\\(|__NR|asm\\(|\" .* \"|brk|sbrk|gettimeofday|getpid|open|read|write|close|lseek|exit|fstat|stat|mmap|munmap|ioctl\" doomgeneric/doomgeneric/my_stdlib.c | head -120\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,120p' doomgeneric/doomgeneric/my_stdlib.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '121,260p' doomgeneric/doomgeneric/my_stdlib.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
